soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: the display clocks go off whenever no MIPS runs at the standby

suspend_late gated the display clocks of a core that was not running
only when an earlier standby had parked it. A restart that fails after
its park sequence leaves the core parked without that mark, and the next
standby then let the pipeline of the old firmware run through the
self-refresh - fault B (review finding CC-2). Gating a pipeline that
never ran saves and writes back the same words, so the clocks now go off
whenever no core runs.

Checked offline with the review's harness (case T3: gated=1, all other
cases unchanged); not measured on the device, it needs two faults in a
row. arbeit/review-r2-20261009/FUNDE.md CC-2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -2428,9 +2428,13 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 		return 0;
 	cpu_comm_s2r_count++;
 	if (!cpu_comm_mips_running()) {
-		/* parked since an earlier sleep: its pipeline still runs */
-		if (READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since))
-			cpu_comm_disp_gate(dev);
+		/*
+		 * Parked since an earlier sleep, or held after a restart that
+		 * failed past its park: the pipeline the old firmware set up
+		 * still runs either way. Gating a pipeline that never ran
+		 * saves and writes back the same words.
+		 */
+		cpu_comm_disp_gate(dev);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
